# Approach
<!-- Describe your approach to solving the problem. -->
- Find the breakpoint(position where n[i]<n[i+1])
- Then find the element which greater than breakpoint but is the smallest
- Swap the variables i.e breakpoint and the other variable which we have find
- Then reverse the remaning array 

# Complexity
- Time complexity:
<!-- Add your time complexity here, e.g. $$O(n)$$ -->
O(3N)

- Space complexity:
<!-- Add your space complexity here, e.g. $$O(n)$$ -->
