# Approach
<!-- Describe your approach to solving the problem. -->
- Find the breakpoint(position where n[i]<n[i+1])
- Then find the element which greater than breakpoint but is the smallest
- Swap the variables i.e breakpoint and the other variable which we have find
- Then reverse the remaning array 

# Complexity
- Time complexity:
<!-- Add your time complexity here, e.g. $$O(n)$$ -->
O(3N)

- Space complexity:
<!-- Add your space complexity here, e.g. $$O(n)$$ -->
O(1)
# Code
```
class Solution {
    public void nextPermutation(int[] n) {
        //breakpoint
       if(  n==null || n.length<=1)return;

		int i = n.length-2;

		while(i>=0 && n[i]>=n[i+1])i--;

		int j=n.length-1;

		if(i>=0) {
			while(n[j]<=n[i])j--;
			swap(n,i,j);
		}

		reverse(n,i+1,n.length-1);

		for(int p=0;p<n.length;p++) {
			System.out.println(n[p]);
		}

	}
	public static void swap(int n[],int i,int j) {
		int temp=n[i];
		n[i]=n[j];
		n[j]=temp;
	}
	public static void reverse(int n[],int i,int j) {
		while(i<j) {
			swap(n,i,j);
			i++;
			j--;
		}
	}
}
```

