# Approach
<!-- Describe your approach to solving the problem. -->
We have to find a triplet of (i, j, k) such that 
i<j<k , 
nums[j] - nums[i] == diff, and 
nums[k] - nums[j] == diff

in other word we can also say nums[k]-nums[i]== 2*diff. To reduce the time complexity I use only 2 loop remove the loop for k and include it in j iterartion such that nums[j]-nums[i] == 2*diff. So in every iterartion of j we will get 2 condition nums[j]-nums[i] == diff and nums[j]-nums[i] == 2*diff when these 2 condition get satisfied in j iterartion, We get 1 count as answer. So for every iteration when count>=2 we add 1 to ans and at last return it.

# Complexity
- Time complexity: O(n^2)
